{title: Winter Wonderland}

{capo-guitar: 1}

{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[Amaj7]Sleigh bells ring, are you [A6]listenin',
[A#dim7]In the [Bm7]lane, snow is [Bm6]glistenin'
A [E7]Beautiful [Bm7]sight,
We're [E7]happy ton[Bm6]ight,
[E]Walking in a [E7]winter wonder[Amaj7]land.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[Amaj7]Gone away is the [A6]bluebird,
[A#dim7]Here to [Bm7]stay is a [Bm6]new bird,
He [E7]sings a love [Bm7]song,
As [E7]we go a[Bm6]long,
[E]Walking in a [E7]winter wonder[Amaj7]land.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus 1"}

[C#maj7/G#]In the meadow [F#maj7]we can build a [C#maj7]snowman,
[C#maj7/G#]Then pretend that [F#maj7]he is Parson [C#maj7]Brown
[E]He'll say, "Are you [A]married?" We'll say, "[E]No, man!"
But [G#dim7]you can do the [B7]job
When you're in [E]town. [E+]

{end_of_chorus}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

[Amaj7]Later on, we'll con[A6]spire,
[A#dim7]As we [Bm7]dream by the [Bm6]fire
To [E7]face unafraid, [Bm7]
The [E7]plans that we've [Bm6]made,
[E]Walking in a [E7]winter wonder[Amaj7]land.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus 2"}

[C#maj7/G#]In the meadow [F#maj7]we can build a [C#maj7]snowman,
[C#maj7/G#]And pretend that he's a [F#maj7]circus [C#maj7]clown
[E]We'll have lots of [A]fun with mister [E]snowman,
Un[G#dim7]til the other [B7]kiddies knock him [E]down [E+]

{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}

[Amaj7]When it snows, ain't it [A6]thrillin',
[A#dim7]Though your [Bm7]nose gets a [Bm6]chillin'
We'll [E7]frolic and play, [Bm7]
The [E7]Eskimo [Bm6]way,
[E]Walking in a [E7]winter wonder[Amaj7]land.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_outro}

[Amaj7]Walking [A#dim7]in a [Bm7]winter [E]wonder[Amaj7]land,
[E]Walking in a [E+]winter wonder[Amaj7]land.

{end_of_outro}
